ntdll: Run Windows child processes as threads of the app.

With KITSUNE_THREADED_PROCESS, ios_spawn_threaded_child starts a child
as threads of the app. Each child gets its own PEB and process context
(ios_process_context.h), maps its own ntdll through the image factory
(ios_ntdll_image.h), publishes its own callbacks and uses its own
PEB-owned fd cache (ios_fd_cache.h, KITSUNE_PROCESS_CACHE_EXPERIMENT).
When a child exits, a reaper thread joins its threads and releases its
state. loader.c also starts the in-process server, loads unix libraries
from the app bundle and logs the boot steps. debug.c writes output for
host threads Wine did not create; thread.c dumps registers, stack and
objects for an unhandled exception.

The PEB-owned fd cache is adapted from Madeira (willfaust/Madeira
9dc2324).
---
